-- An IMPORT that resolves to nothing, WITH a rule in this module that reads a
-- name the import was meant to supply. Both errors below are expected, and the
-- order they are written in is the point of the fixture: the IMPORT error says
-- what is wrong, and the undefined identifier under it is the SYMPTOM that used
-- to be the only thing a reader saw (smucclaw/l4-ide#971).
--
-- `zz-no-such-module-971` is deliberately the name of nothing: no file in this
-- directory, no stdlib module, nothing in any ambient tier. The golden therefore
-- records every location the resolver probed -- including two machine-global
-- ones -- which is why `mkPathScrubber` in jl4/tests/Main.hs has to scrub the
-- XDG store and the executable's own directory as well as the two prefixes it
-- scrubbed before.
--
-- Its twin is `unresolved-unreferenced.l4`, which references nothing and so
-- typechecks; between them they pin that a bad IMPORT fails in both cases.

IMPORT `zz-no-such-module-971`

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cost of` amount MEANS amount TIMES `the missing rate`
